<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mir Nasir of Bandar Rig</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mir Nasir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandar-rig">Bandar Rig</a> was the Arab lord of the port of Bandar Rig on the Persian shore of the Gulf in the mid-18th century. A member of the Za'ab family, he governed the town independently after central authority collapsed on the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> in 1747, and dealt with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> on nearby Kharg. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mir-muhanna">Mir Muhanna</a> became a notorious raider of Gulf shipping.</p></div>
